<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Foundation: Attention as a Latent-Memory Operator</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We briefly recap the base architecture to establish notation.
Table <a href="#S3.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 3 Foundation: Attention as a Latent-Memory Operator ‣ A Miniature Brain Transformer:Thalamic Gating, Hippocampal Lateralization, AmygdaloidSalience, and Prefrontal Working Memory inAttention-Coupled Latent Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> summarises all recurring symbols used throughout the paper.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span><span id="S3.T2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Notation.</span> All symbols used in equations throughout the paper.
Learned parameters are marked <math id="S3.T2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dagger" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>†</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dagger</annotation></semantics></math>; running/state buffers are marked <math id="S3.T2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\star" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋆</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\star</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
