<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>The miniature brain architecture.
Five neuroscientifically motivated modules are connected through the <math id="S9.F2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\top}\!AVW" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\top}\!AVW</annotation></semantics></math>
write-back operator.
Solid arrows show the primary information flow; dashed red arrows show callosal
inhibitory cross-talk; dotted blue arrows show modulatory signals.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S9.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S9.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 9 Unified Forward Pass: The Miniature Brain ‣ A Miniature Brain Transformer:Thalamic Gating, Hippocampal Lateralization, AmygdaloidSalience, and Prefrontal Working Memory inAttention-Coupled Latent Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> summarises the parameter overhead of each new module.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S9.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>Complete set of learnable parameters added by the four new modules over the base lateral model. Full model total: <math id="S9.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3{,}716{,}615" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3,716,615</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3{,}716{,}615</annotation></semantics></math> parameters.</figcaption>
<table id="S9.T3.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
